            "portrait": "James embodies the loyal butler deeply rooted in the traditions of service and protocol. His formal, clipped manner and dry humor resonate with the steadfast values of a bygone era, resistant to the rapid social changes around him. His internal conflict about the stability of household order reflects the uncertainty many long-serving staff faced as the social fabric shifted during the 1930s.",
            "eraIntersection": "His anxiety over changing household dynamics mirrors broader societal tensions between tradition and modernity in interwar Britain."
          },
