        "revealImplications": "The final revelation retroactively casts the early witness statements scene in a new light, showing how natural phenomena misled perceptions and testimony. The discovery of mechanical tampering in the library reveals the calculated manipulation of time, which reframes the seemingly solid alibis and household schedules introduced mid-story. Additionally, the servant ledger’s overlapping and inconsistent entries gain significance as deliberate cover-ups, clarifying why initial suspect accusations were misdirected and highlighting the intricate social engineering behind the murder’s concealment. Taken together, these implications should be treated as cumulative pressure that reshapes how each suspect interprets risk, loyalty, and consequence over the final act.",
